# Alexandria — Cursor Rules

## Project
Alexandria is JDA's AI-native operational platform. This repo has two deployables:
- **The Portal** (repo root) — Next.js 16 App Router admin app. The live app is the `(portal)` route group.
- **The Bridge** (`mcp/`) — a standalone MCP server (`mcp/src/index.ts`) exposing `alexandria_*` tools to Claude.

TypeScript strict mode throughout. Tailwind CSS v4. Path alias `@/*` → `src/*`.

## Leftover starter code — do not build on it
This repo was forked from a Next.js + Sanity starter. These files are unused by the live app:
- `src/components/modules/`, `src/components/global/`, `src/components/PageBuilder.tsx`
Ignore them. If they get in the way, prefer deleting over extending.

## File structure
- Portal pages: `src/app/(portal)/` — all share `(portal)/layout.tsx`
- JSON API routes: `src/app/api/`
- Portal UI components: `src/components/portal/`
- UI primitives: `src/components/ui/` — one directory per component, `index.tsx` default export, optional `types.ts`
- Postgres access: `src/lib/db.ts` (connection) + `src/lib/schema.ts` (queries + `migrate()`)
- Auth: `src/lib/auth.ts`, gate enforced by `src/middleware.ts`
- Sanity: schemas in `src/sanity/schemas/`, queries in `src/sanity/lib/queries.ts`, client in `src/sanity/lib/client.ts`

## Data — two stores
- **Postgres** holds users, roles, permissions, sessions, intake & feedback.
- **Sanity** holds editorial content (methodologies, templates, brand packages, capabilities, platform guide).
- Fetch Sanity content ONLY in server components, via `sanityFetch()` from `@/sanity/lib/client`. Never fetch in client components — pass data as props.
- GROQ queries use tagged template literals.

## Database migrations
- There is NO migration tool. The schema IS the idempotent statements in `migrate()`.
- To change the schema, add `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` / `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` statements to `migrate()` — `src/lib/schema.ts` for portal tables, `mcp/src/index.ts` for Bridge tables.
- Never assume a fresh database; existing deployments re-run `migrate()`.

## Auth
- One auth gate: Azure AD `Alexandria-Users` group membership (`GROUP_USERS` constant).
- Authorization (`account_type`, roles, `role_permissions`) is app-managed in Postgres — never derive it from Azure.
- The Azure Object ID (`oid`) is the stable user key: `session.user.id` and `users.object_id`.

## MCP server
- The entire Bridge is one file: `mcp/src/index.ts`. Tools are registered with `server.tool(...)`.
- Adding/removing a tool requires practitioners to reconnect the connector — note this when you do.

## Components
- Default exports only. Props interface named `[ComponentName]Props`.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional Tailwind classes.

## Styling
- Tailwind utility classes only. No CSS modules or styled-components.
- Theme tokens in the `@theme` block of `src/app/globals.css`; portal UI also uses `var(--color-jda-*)` CSS variables. Never hardcode colors.
- Map enum-like DB/Sanity values to display strings via `src/lib/portal-labels.ts`.
- Mobile-first responsive (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).

## TypeScript
- Strict mode. Never use `any`.
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes.

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML landmarks; keyboard-accessible interactive elements; ARIA on custom widgets.

## Avoid
- Pages Router (App Router only)
- Fetching Sanity data in client components
- `use client` unless genuinely needed for interactivity
- Hardcoded strings and colors
- Building on the leftover starter code listed above
